            <ArticleTitle>Colocolic intussusception caused by pneumatosis cystoides coli.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>392-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 29-year-old man with a long-standing history of abdominal pain related to an intermittent colocolic intussusception caused by pneumatosis cystoides coli. To our knowledge, only one similar case has been reported in the English-language literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
